    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Neovascular age-related macular degeneration, left eye, inactive on treat-and-extend (H35.3221)</content>. Dry after eight weeks (central subfield thickness 268 µm), with acuity 70 letters, up 15 from baseline. Fourth injection given today without complication. [S]<list><item>Extend the next interval to ten weeks.</item><item>Same-day call for new distortion or warning signs.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Intermediate dry age-related macular degeneration, right eye (H35.3112)</content>. Stable: 77 letters, no fluid on OCT, no change on Amsler checks. [S]<list><item>Continue the AREDS2 supplement, daily Amsler checks, and dilated examination at each retina visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Best-corrected visual acuity (ETDRS letters)</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>77 letters right and 70 letters left</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Optical coherence tomography of the macula</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Both eyes. Left dry at 268 µm; right drusen without fluid</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Intraocular pressure before and after injection</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Before injection 15 mmHg in each eye; after injection, optic nerve perfused and counting fingers</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Dilated examination of the fellow (right) eye</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Large drusen unchanged; no fluid on OCT</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Comprehensive dilated eye examination</td><td>Every 1 to 2 years at 65 or older</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Both eyes examined in full at the March retina consultation and again today</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Intravitreal injection safety</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Fourth injection; no complication to date</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Teaching on warning signs of endophthalmitis and retinal detachment</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Reviewed again before the ten-week interval</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Daily home Amsler grid, each eye</td><td>Daily</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Daily checks recorded; no change in either eye</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>AREDS2 supplement for intermediate AMD</td><td>Daily, long term</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taking it daily</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Low-vision rehabilitation, with home fall-risk review and a driving assessment</td><td>Once central vision is reduced; review as vision changes</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Completed since the last visit: lighting, magnifier, and labels in place; cleared for short local daytime driving. Review if vision changes</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Functional vision assessment (reading, color, driving, work)</td><td>At diagnosis; again with change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Painting daily with aids; reading with the magnifier; daytime local driving only</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>At follow-up, because vision loss raises the risk of depression; periodically at 65 or older</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Score 0, down from 1 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive screen (Mini-Cog)</td><td>Annually at 65 or older</td><td>Up to date</td><td>5 of 5 at intake in March; next at the annual wellness visit</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Gain at least 10 ETDRS letters in the left eye by the end of the loading phase. Outcome by 1968-05-07: Left eye improved from 55 to 69 letters after three injections [S]</item><item>Dry macula on OCT (central subfield thickness below 300 um, no fluid) by the end of the loading phase. Outcome by 1968-05-07: Central subfield thickness fell from 418 to 274 um with no fluid [S]</item><item>Check the Amsler grid daily for each eye and report any change the same day. Outcome by 1968-07-02: Daily checks recorded; no new change in the right eye [S]</item><item>Complete a low-vision rehabilitation evaluation and set up studio lighting and magnification by the July visit. Outcome by 1968-07-02: Task lighting, a stand magnifier, and high-contrast labels in place; still painting daily [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Age-Related Macular Degeneration Preferred Practice Pattern (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, cataract and glaucoma monographs (eye-examination items) (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Retina visit in ten weeks for acuity, OCT, pressure, and the fifth injection. Annual wellness visit in the fall. Next scheduled visit 1968-10-15: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
